# CircuitPython Conventions

## Runtime Environment

Code runs on CircuitPython 9.2.0 (not CPython). Key constraints:
- ~8 MB PSRAM available; ~7.4 MB free after framebuffer
- No pip/venv — libraries are built into the firmware or copied to `CIRCUITPY/lib/`
- Entry point is `code.py` on the CIRCUITPY drive; auto-reloads on file save
- Multi-file projects: put modules in CIRCUITPY root, import normally
- Use `tio /dev/tty.usbmodem*` for serial console (not Cursor integrated terminal)

## Core Libraries

| Module | Purpose |
|--------|---------|
| `board` | Pin definitions for Qualia S3 (`TFT_PINS`, `TFT_IO_EXPANDER`, `SCL`, `SDA`) |
| `busio` | I2C bus access (`busio.I2C`) |
| `displayio` | Bitmap, TileGrid, Group, Palette, ColorConverter |
| `bitmaptools` | Fast C-level `fill_region()`, `draw_line()` — always prefer over pixel loops |
| `framebufferio` | `FramebufferDisplay` for DotClock-backed displays |
| `dotclockframebuffer` | Parallel RGB TTL framebuffer and `ioexpander_send_init_sequence` |
| `adafruit_focaltouch` | FocalTech FT6x36 touch driver (in `lib/`, address `0x38`) |
| `adafruit_display_text` | Text labels via `label.Label` with `terminalio.FONT` |
| `terminalio` | Built-in font, no extra files needed |

## Display Initialization Pattern

```python
from displayio import release_displays
release_displays()  # always call first

i2c = busio.I2C(board.SCL, board.SDA, frequency=400_000)
tft_io_expander = dict(board.TFT_IO_EXPANDER)
dotclockframebuffer.ioexpander_send_init_sequence(i2c, init_sequence, **tft_io_expander)
i2c.deinit()  # deinit after init sequence

fb = dotclockframebuffer.DotClockFramebuffer(**dict(board.TFT_PINS), **tft_timings)
display = FramebufferDisplay(fb, auto_refresh=False, rotation=90)  # landscape
```

## Touch Initialization (after display)

```python
i2c = busio.I2C(board.SCL, board.SDA, frequency=400_000)
touch = adafruit_focaltouch.Adafruit_FocalTouch(i2c, address=0x38)
# Do NOT deinit i2c — touch needs it continuously
```

## Syntax Limitations

- f-strings do not support ternary expressions: `f"{x if y else z}"` causes SyntaxError
- f-string line continuation with `f"..." f"..."` on separate lines is not supported
- Workaround: compute values into variables before the f-string

## Performance Guidelines

- Always use `bitmaptools.fill_region()` for rectangles — 43-46x faster than pixel loops
- Use `displayio.Palette` + palette indices instead of `ColorConverter` + raw RGB565
- `Palette.make_transparent(index)` enables sprite transparency over backgrounds
- `displayio.Group(scale=N)` scales sprites without redraw cost
- Moving `Group.x`/`Group.y` or `TileGrid.x`/`TileGrid.y` is instant (no redraw)
- `TileGrid.flip_x` mirrors sprites without redraw
- Target ~30ms sleep for ~32 FPS game loops
- Use `auto_refresh=False` during batch bitmap writes, then `True` to flush

## Deployment

- `circup install <library>` to install libs to board (requires `pipx install circup`)
- `circup` needs `~/.local/bin` on PATH
- Copy `.py` modules to CIRCUITPY root for imports
- Writing to CIRCUITPY triggers auto-reload; `tio` may disconnect briefly during writes
- Rev A IO expander at `0x3f` (default); Rev B at `0x38` (conflicts with touch)
